<description>&lt;p&gt;Rival jihadist groups JNIM and ISSP are clashing in northern Burkina Faso as the state loses ground, while bandits in Niger State killed two kidnapping victims despite a six-million-naira ransom payment. Gunmen ambushed a market convoy in western Niger, killing at least 38 civilians. In Nigeria, the army reported killing eight terrorists and rescuing 125 kidnap victims in nationwide operations. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxPZ28ta0Q5dlJhVGJLQ2JOQUctdkQ1T1VzbTA1TEhTWjBYVTZMdnV2LTRCZFd3bEZhcmtZTVg5STdSVDZDdlBkN3hwOTh4UjJYb3hBYkc0NlRSYUE4RjQyRFhJMFFJeEZCYkxlUm53N0VqQnl0X2xqeWZuRXFjV2xTMDJBZGdiUnhJVmpXcnVXQnJwVVd5eklhdVlkVENNZXJyTTRaVDRBRktqNVI5emhCcEtiOXpIYmJfRkhNWERzaW4?oc=5&quot;&gt;Anadolu Ajansı&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxPck1idk1lUEtQcmZwQnhkLS1EZ3pKaVhEYWVDMERmODMtUUNEUDdqTVR6S2xZNEFxTTRkZm9aZ1Zueld2X0drWVpIQkt2TUZDeFgtTUU1UktyaF91X1piWFdZRnVXcTl1T25uNEZSTW9HV0MybUVUN1FlSWxOS1hTdE9xMlJrMmNTLWJhSHpPUmhvYWVJNm92YXpwSlVaUnRFdzV1SzgzZEVzNzN2WlZyQk13?oc=5&quot;&gt;Ahram Online&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZ0FVX3lxTE9RbnlJSl9FUWp0WmZqUXBTNC16SktxYi1ZN2NMcFc4aVNtc1NTbFBHR3BKX0dDbjV0TnF6bHVlSkJPamF5QUZKbzVjNnFweTF6T0luQ00zVlhPNkNXTzREeUo5Vksxc2M?oc=5&quot;&gt;Envanter Medya&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxOSGs3X3NFbXZ6ckVtTkEwVzZIdGhRTjVzLVhYVHhuN0ZrWHRYTFJrLU5FbGVDRG9yUVJtRmZCUENRandfb0FEdENSU3IxMWtfVHQxZHZkcHdVWG50WExZVWxmbE91N044bGkwUnZDZ0FybnV1YnpwZS1jWnNxMDE2QnoyaFlZUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Post Nigeria&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUx